{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"hedonistic-historical-graywolf","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n- navapbc/homebrew-rebar `.github/workflows/autobump.yml` (workflow id 316476444) is in state `disabled_inactivity` (checked 2026-11-09). Its last run was a scheduled run on 2026-10-28 23:31 PDT.\n- `Formula/rebar.rb` still points at the nava_rebar-0.13.1 sdist, although 0.14.0 was published to PyPI on 2026-10-30. The runbook's claim that the 6-hourly schedule self-heals a missed release does not hold while the workflow is disabled.\n- GitHub disables scheduled workflows after 60 days with no repository activity. The tap's own bot commits apparently do not keep it active, because it only commits when a bump happens.\n\n## Impact\nHomebrew users stay 2 releases behind (0.13.1 while 0.14.0 and 0.15.0 are on PyPI), and `gh workflow run autobump.yml` (runbook step 3) cannot be dispatched.\n\n## Remediation (operator)\nRe-enable the workflow (`gh workflow enable autobump.yml --repo navapbc/homebrew-rebar`), then dispatch it. Separately, decide how to stop the inactivity disable from recurring (for example a keepalive, or moving the trigger into rebar's release.yml), and correct docs/releasing.md step 3.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [non-codebase] autobump.yml is enabled and Formula/rebar.rb points at the latest PyPI sdist.\n      provenance: environment=github.com navapbc/homebrew-rebar; principal=JoeOakhartNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read via gh api of the workflow state and the formula contents\n- [ ] docs/releasing.md step 3 states the inactivity-disable failure mode and its recovery.","id":"ed54-92ac-4700-43b1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Homebrew tap autobump disabled for inactivity; formula stuck at 0.13.1, missed 0.14.0"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794256240331546001,"uuid":"173c4f31-62cd-4c86-895e-5b23864243f3"}